3. Data loaded at runtime

Prices, company data, logos, option chains, news, filings, portraits of
members of Congress and prediction market data are fetched from third
parties while the app runs. They are not part of this repository and not
covered by its licence; the terms of each source apply.

Financial disclosure reports of members of the US House of Representatives
(Clerk of the House), the US Senate (eFD system), the President and Vice
President (U.S. Office of Government Ethics) and further members of the US
administration (OGE Form 278-T, listed by the U.S. Office of Government
Ethics and the White House, whitehouse.gov) must not be used, under
5 U.S.C. § 13107, for any unlawful purpose, for any commercial purpose other
than by news and communications media for dissemination to the general
public, for determining or establishing anyone's credit rating, or directly
or indirectly for soliciting money for any political, charitable or other
purpose. This program is a free learning and practice tool. If you build on
it, you are responsible for complying with these terms. The 278-T reports of
further members of the administration are fetched on the user's device only,
for personal use; none of them is part of this program.

Reports of managers' transactions (Art. 19 MAR) and of major holdings of
voting rights (sections 33 et seq. WpHG) come from the databases of the
German Federal Financial Supervisory Authority. Source:
© Bundesanstalt für Finanzdienstleistungsaufsicht / www.bafin.de
A snapshot is bundled in app/src/main/assets/copytrading/bafin.json
(tools/bafin/holen.py); the app adds newer reports while it runs.

US insider transactions (Form 4) come from the Form 345 data sets and
EDGAR of the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (public records of the
US government). A snapshot is bundled in app/src/main/assets/copytrading/
sec.json (tools/sec/holen.py), together with a condensed purchase history
since 2016 in sec_historie.json (tools/sec/historie.py). Notices of proposed sales (Form 144) and
reports of beneficial ownership (Schedule 13D and 13G) come from SEC EDGAR as
well; they are fetched at runtime for the opened stock with the user's contact
address and are not bundled.

Swedish insider transactions (Art. 19 MAR) come from the public insider
register of Finansinspektionen (fi.se). A snapshot is bundled in
app/src/main/assets/copytrading/insider_se.json (tools/schweden/holen.py);
the app adds newer reports while it runs.

Net short positions in shares traded in Paris come from the list of the
Autorité des marchés financiers published on data.gouv.fr under the
Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0
(https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence). The data was
summarised per share (open positions and weekly totals);
app/src/main/assets/copytrading/leerpositionen_fr.json is built with
tools/amf/holen.py and the app recalculates it from the current list.

Commitments of Traders data comes from the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading
Commission (public records of the US government) and is fetched at runtime.

Further insider transactions: app/src/main/assets/copytrading/insider_fr.json
(© Autorité des marchés financiers – droits réservés, BDIF) and insider_nl.json
(Autoriteit Financiële Markten, register of managers' transactions) are built
with the desktop task insiderBuendel; the app adds newer reports at runtime.
Swiss management transactions (SIX Exchange Regulation) are fetched at runtime
only. Issuer announcements of the officially appointed mechanism of Česká
národní banka (Czechia, oam.cnb.cz), the officially appointed mechanism of the
Luxembourg Stock Exchange (luxse.com, read on the device without links to its
website), 1Info (Computershare, Italy), the Public OAM of the Cyprus Stock
Exchange, Dealings by Directors of the Colombo Stock Exchange (Sri Lanka) and
Major Investors Trade Activities of Muscat Clearing & Depository (Oman) are
fetched on the user's device for the opened stock only, for personal use. For
the capital market disclosures of Magyar Nemzeti Bank (Hungary) the app reads
only the search results and links each disclosure; the user opens the PDF
files there. UK director
dealings come from Investegate (investegate.co.uk) after a one-time
confirmation as a private investor, and managers' transactions in Denmark,
Finland, Iceland and the Baltic states from the news interface of Nasdaq
Nordic; both are fetched on the user's device for personal use. HKEX (Hong
Kong) is linked only. If a source returns nothing, the app links the National
Storage Mechanism of the Financial Conduct Authority (UK) or the Nasdaq Nordic
page. Lists and forms the user downloads
personally (BSE India, Consob Italy, net short positions of the Bundesanzeiger
and of the Financial Conduct Authority, SEDI weekly summaries converted with
tools/kanada/sedi.py, reports of the Egyptian Exchange, Nigerian Exchange,
Boursa Kuwait and Qatar Stock Exchange, Appendix 3Y forms of the ASX,
notifications under Art. 19 MAR as PDF) can be imported in the app and stay on
the device; none of these data is part of this program. The app does not open
or link the website of the Qatar Stock Exchange. Lobby registers:
app/src/main/assets/behoerden/lobby_welt.json is built with tools/lobby/welt.py
from the EU Transparency Register (reuse under Commission Decision 2011/833/EU),
the lobby register of the German Bundestag and the HATVP register of interest
representatives (Licence Ouverte).

Short positions in Swedish shares come from the Blankningsregister of
Finansinspektionen (open data, source and date stated);
app/src/main/assets/copytrading/leerpositionen_se.json is built with
tools/fi_blankning/holen.py. UK aggregated net short positions are read only
from the files the user downloads from the Financial Conduct Authority.

Euro area yield curves (dataset YC) and the Harmonised Index of Consumer
Prices of the euro area (dataset HICP) come from the ECB Data Portal of the
European Central Bank. US consumer prices (CPI-U) of the U.S. Bureau of Labor
Statistics are fetched through FRED (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis) or
the BLS interface. BLS.gov cannot vouch for the data or analyses derived from
these data after the data have been retrieved from BLS.gov. ETF holdings (topHoldings), annual report figures
(fundamentals-timeseries), similar stocks (recommendationsbysymbol) and stock
splits come from Yahoo Finance. All of these are fetched at runtime only and
are not bundled.

The LuSE All Share Index (Lusaka Securities Exchange, luse.co.zm) is read at
runtime from the public market data page of the exchange for personal use,
with the source stated; nothing is bundled.

FDA approvals and recalls come from openFDA (U.S. Food and Drug Administration,
CC0 1.0) and are fetched at runtime. openFDA is not intended for medical
decisions.

13F holdings come from SEC EDGAR filings (public records of the US
government) and 13f.info. Official congressional portraits come from
unitedstates.github.io and are in the public domain.


Lobbying reports (LD-2) are public records filed with the Clerk of the US
House of Representatives; app/src/main/assets/behoerden/lobbying.json is a
summary of them per company. app/src/main/assets/copytrading/haus.json and
vermoegen.json are built from the financial disclosure reports published by
the Clerk of the House and fall under the terms of 5 U.S.C. § 13107 above.
Federal contract data comes from USAspending.gov, short selling data from
FINRA, campaign finance data from the Federal Election Commission, and
patent data from the USPTO Open Data Portal; all of it is fetched at runtime.
Public contract awards come from TED (Tenders Electronic Daily, reuse under
Commission Decision 2011/833/EU) and from Contracts Finder (Open Government
Licence v3.0, https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/),
also fetched at runtime. app/src/main/assets/firmen/staatsgeld-eu.json
summarises grants of the EU budget per company from the Financial
Transparency System of the European Commission, licensed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

app/src/main/assets/behoerden/entlassungen.json contains layoff notices from
WARN Feed (https://github.com/APVentureEngine/warn-act-notices), licensed
under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The data was
filtered to companies in the app's catalogue and shortened. WARN Feed
collects the notices from state labour agencies; it is not affiliated with
this program.

Electricity (fetched at runtime only, none bundled): generation by source and
consumption in Germany from SMARD, attributed to "Bundesnetzagentur | SMARD.de"
(CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). With the user's
own token, day-ahead prices per bidding zone from the ENTSO-E
Transparency Platform (named as the source); the app does not ship a token.
The last retrieved values are kept on the device.

Early signals and outlook (fetched at runtime only, none bundled): weekly
inventories and historical futures prices of the U.S. Energy Information
Administration (eia.gov), initial claims of the U.S. Department of Labor
through FRED, checkpoint travel numbers of the Transportation Security
Administration (tsa.gov), the U.S. Drought Monitor (jointly produced by the
National Drought Mitigation Center at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln,
the United States Department of Agriculture and the National Oceanic and
Atmospheric Administration) and, with the user's own free key, EU gas
storage data of GIE AGSI+ (Gas Infrastructure Europe, named as the source).
Fed funds futures of CME Group come through Yahoo Finance, US gross domestic
product for the Buffett indicator from the World Bank (CC BY 4.0). The St. Louis
Fed Financial Stress Index and the ICE BofA US High Yield Index Option-Adjusted
Spread (ICE Data Indices, LLC) are retrieved from FRED, Federal Reserve Bank of
St. Louis. Press releases of the Deutsche Bundesbank come from its RSS feeds
(source: Deutsche Bundesbank). FRED content is held in memory only while a
view is open; it is never stored or cached, and each series is cited in the
source list of the page as "<owner>, <series>, retrieved from FRED, Federal
Reserve Bank of St. Louis". The running GDP estimate GDPNow is read from the
spreadsheet of the Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta (atlantafed.org, (c)
Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta, not bundled, not stored) with FRED as fallback.
app/src/main/assets/indikatoren holds hit rates computed from such series
and from prices, and the long series listed in section 5. Mentions on Reddit and 4chan /biz/
come from ApeWisdom (apewisdom.io), page views from the Wikimedia REST API.

Replacement sources for data whose original source cannot be fetched (all of
them fetched at runtime only, none bundled):
- Newer US Senate transaction reports come from the open dataset Congress
  Trading Monitor (https://github.com/kadoa-org/congress-trading-monitor,
  MIT licence, Copyright (c) Kadoa). It is read from the same Senate eFD
  filings and falls under the terms of 5 U.S.C. § 13107 above. Only the
  Senate rows are used, not the returns or prices of the project.
- The cyclically adjusted price/earnings ratio (CAPE) comes from the data
  of Robert J. Shiller (https://shillerdata.com). Neither he nor his
  affiliates guarantee its accuracy.
- The Global Supply Chain Pressure Index: © Federal Reserve Bank of New
  York. Content from the New York Fed subject to the Terms of Use at
  newyorkfed.org.
- Margin loans of brokers and dealers (Federal Reserve, Financial Accounts
  of the United States, Z.1), the Freight Transportation Services Index
  and rail freight carloads (U.S. Bureau of Transportation Statistics) and
  industrial production of semiconductors (Federal Reserve) are fetched
  through FRED, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis; these series are in the
  public domain.
- Story counts from the Hacker News search API (hn.algolia.com) and
  hashtag usage counts of mastodon.social (numbers only, no posts) are
  fetched for the opened stock.

Further sources (fetched at runtime on the user's device for personal,
non-commercial use only, kept in memory, none bundled):
- Put/call ratios of the last trading day from the daily market statistics
  of Cboe Global Markets (cdn.cboe.com); no history is stored. For the
  look back the app loads the archive file of the equity put/call ratio
  (2006 to 2019) from the same site on the device and keeps it in memory
  only; it is not part of the app.
- Settlement prices of the VX futures from the Cboe Futures Exchange
  (cdn.cboe.com) for the VIX futures curve; only shown, no history is stored.
- The CNN Fear & Greed Index (CNN, through the interface its website uses)
  and the weekly AAII Sentiment Survey (American Association of Individual
  Investors, aaii.com).
- World Container Index assessed by Drewry (drewry.co.uk), credited to
  Drewry; weekly rail traffic figures of the Association of American
  Railroads (aar.org); worldwide semiconductor billings from the Historical
  Billings Report of World Semiconductor Trade Statistics (wsts.org),
  © WSTS.
- Factor returns for the factor breakdown of the portfolio: the monthly
  Fama/French five factors and the momentum factor for the US from the
  Kenneth R. French Data Library
  (https://mba.tuck.dartmouth.edu/pages/faculty/ken.french/data_library.html),
  Copyright Eugene F. Fama and Kenneth R. French; and the market and theme
  factors per region from Global Factor Data (https://jkpfactors.com/) by
  Theis Ingerslev Jensen, Bryan Kelly and Lasse Heje Pedersen, licensed
  under CC BY-NC 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/).
  The app computes regressions from them and shows the results only.
- Insider disclosures of Boursa Kuwait through its RSS service
  (rss.boursakuwait.com.kw) and the linked disclosure forms.
- With the user's own free token: financial disclosures of US federal
  judges from the CourtListener REST API of the Free Law Project; they fall
  under the terms of 5 U.S.C. § 13107 above.
- With the user's own Bluesky app password: post counts from the Bluesky
  search (numbers only, no posts).
- Letters of fund managers to their investors, read from the senders'
  websites, kept on the device only and shown as excerpts around the
  mention of a stock (two sentences, on request the surrounding paragraph),
  with a link to the sender; with the user's contact
  address also fund reports from the EDGAR full-text search of the SEC.
- Crypto funding rates and open interest from the public interfaces of Kraken
  Futures (https://www.kraken.com/features/futures) and, as fallback, Deribit
  (https://www.deribit.com); stablecoin supply and total value locked from
  DefiLlama (https://defillama.com). Fetched on the device, shown with the
  source named on the page, nothing stored.


